From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ole32: Succeed in IPropertyStorage::SetTimes on a simple property set.

IPropertyStorage::SetTimes succeeds on a property set of a compound file
(it returned E_NOTIMPL): only a nonsimple property set has times, those of
its storage, and a simple set (the only kind Wine makes) keeps none, as the
ole32 property tests show on Windows. A todo_wine goes.

Gate: test/ole32-proptimes-gate.sh.
---
 dlls/ole32/stg_prop.c       | 8 +++++++-
 dlls/ole32/tests/stg_prop.c | 1 -
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ole32/stg_prop.c b/dlls/ole32/stg_prop.c
index 53aa2df..81e5e13 100644
--- a/dlls/ole32/stg_prop.c
+++ b/dlls/ole32/stg_prop.c
@@ -1088,8 +1088,14 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI IPropertyStorage_fnSetTimes(
     const FILETIME* patime,
     const FILETIME* pmtime)
 {
-    FIXME("\n");
+    TRACE("%p, %p, %p, %p\n", iface, pctime, patime, pmtime);
+
+    /* only nonsimple property sets have times, those of their storage; a simple
+     * set (the only kind here) keeps none, and the call succeeds */
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_SETTIMES_NOTIMPL
     return E_NOTIMPL;
+#endif
+    return S_OK;
 }
 
 /************************************************************************
diff --git a/dlls/ole32/tests/stg_prop.c b/dlls/ole32/tests/stg_prop.c
index 0445e44..b165bd0 100644
--- a/dlls/ole32/tests/stg_prop.c
+++ b/dlls/ole32/tests/stg_prop.c
@@ -751,7 +751,6 @@ static void test_propertyset_storage_enum(void)
     memset(&ftime, 0, sizeof(ftime));
     ftime.dwLowDateTime = 1;
     hr = IPropertyStorage_SetTimes(prop_storage, NULL, NULL, &ftime);
-    todo_wine
     ok(hr == S_OK, "Failed to set storage times, hr %#lx.\n", hr);
 
     hr = IEnumSTATPROPSETSTG_Reset(ps_enum);
